
# HPC Cluster Setup Guide

## 1. Install Rocky Linux
- Install Rocky Linux on 3 virtual machines
- Use minimal installation

## 2. Configure Network
- Assign static IPs:
  - Head Node: 192.168.1.10
  - Compute Node 1: 192.168.1.11
  - Compute Node 2: 192.168.1.12

## 3. Set Hostnames
- head-node
- compute-node-1
- compute-node-2

## 4. Configure SSH
- Generate SSH key:
  ssh-keygen
- Copy to nodes:
  ssh-copy-id user@compute-node-1
  ssh-copy-id user@compute-node-2

## 5. Install Packages
sudo dnf install -y gcc make openmpi openmpi-devel slurm nfs-utils

## 6. Configure NFS
- Create shared directory
- Export using /etc/exports

## 7. Configure Slurm
- Setup slurm.conf
- Start services:
  systemctl start slurmctld
  systemctl start slurmd

## 8. Run Jobs
sbatch job_script.sh
